<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:pidyon_haben"><tei:head>REDEMPTION OF THE FIRST-BORN SON</tei:head><tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">Performed on the thirty-first day after birth. Should the child’s father be a kohen or a Levite, or the mother the daughter of a kohen or Levite, they are exempt from this duty. If the thirty-first day falls on a Sabbath or a major festival, the Pidyon ha-Ben is postponed until the following day.</tei:note><tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">Presenting the child to the kohen, the father says:</tei:note><j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:lifecycle/text/pidyon_present"/><tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">Kohen:</tei:note><j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:lifecycle/text/pidyon_question"/><tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">Father:</tei:note><j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:lifecycle/text/pidyon_answer"/><j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:al_pidyon_haben"/><j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:shehecheyanu"/><tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">Holding the redemption-money over the child’s head, the kohen says:</tei:note><j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:lifecycle/text/pidyon_exchange"/><tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">Placing his hand on the child’s head:</tei:note><j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:lifecycle/text/pidyon_child_blessing"/><j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:lifecycle/text/pidyon_closing"/></tei:div>
    </tei:body>
